You can keep it light and simple, then. Tell them about the way games
these days rely on flashy graphics to capture people's interest. Tell
them why you like Nethack. At first glance, it seems like such a
primitive game, doesn't it? Graphics--what graphics? On the surface,
it's yet another dungeon-crawling game.

Why do you like it?

For me, it has this... odd appeal. Other games allow you to save and
restore from any point; there's no risk. In Nethack, I can spend days
carefully building up a character only to lose her through
carelessness or bad luck. In my mind, I know that Nethack's a
single-player dungeon crawl, but it doesn't _feel_ that way--not with
bones files, not with r.g.r.n. posts swapping tips and YASD/YAAP
messages. I've plenty of SDs (none posted, they're too embarrassingly
simple) and not a single AP.

No graphics. Classic gameplay. Nothing really new here--but somehow it
captures our imagination. You can wax lyrical about the images invoked
by the characters and words; I think your teacher might appreciate the
fact that you get adrenalin rushes from plain text... ;)

